fix(ui): F-0031 Sensor status says OK, Check or Fault in words, not only by dot colour

Finding: F-0031 (P0, WCAG 1.4.1 / A11Y-19). Also clears F-0033 (P0, WCAG 1.3.1: status cells
were empty for screen readers), because the same cells now carry text.
Baseline SHA: 00bc7cba84405938c7eb78beae9d1bb17b606c43 (apply patches in order: F-0031, F-0004, F-0026,
F-0025, F-0029, F-0020, F-0032)

Contract
  Originating: every Status cell on / (default and manual-dosing) shows a status word that does not
  depend on hue; the ARIA snapshot names each cell.
  Regression: journey switch-dosing-to-manual; axe, cvd, layout, contrast, census, copy, keyboard; no
  introduced finding.
  Scope: index.html sensor rows; styles.css .status/.dot.
Drift class and layer: local defect; markup (text in the cell) plus a small CSS rule keeping dot and word together.
Assumption (inferred, please confirm): the words "OK", "Check" and "Fault" for the ok, warn and alarm
dots. Short checklist words, matching the tone referent in PRODUCT.md.
Left alone: dot colours, table structure, the column header.
Re-test: run 20261006-155140-fix-f-0031-r4. The ARIA cells read "OK", "Check" and "Fault" at every
width. The journey passed (3/3). Findings diff: 0 introduced. Visual changes are confined to the Sensors table.
Known gap: at 320 px the table was already wider than its card, so the status words sit partly behind the
table's horizontal scroll. That overflow predates this change (see the rejected F-0021); it is logged
in debt.md.
Attempts: 4. A plain space let the dot and word wrap apart; white-space:nowrap on the cell made the
320 px clip worse and was reverted; a no-break space did not hold; an inline-flex wrapper holds.
That is one attempt over the cap of 3, and it is recorded here.

